   The reason I didn't reply was because I know I've seen other regulars
give really good, detailed, step-by-step advice on compiling Nethack, in
the past, and was expecting one of them to post a URL. But in the absence
of any /good/ advice, here's my more-experienced two cents. I've compiled
and patched Nethack a lot, but only for text-mode, never tiles:

   Download DJGPP (www.delorie.com/djgpp; use the Zip Picker).

   Try compiling "Hello World" in C, just to make sure you've got the right 
idea so far.

   Download the DJGPP packages for 'flex', 'bison', 'make', and 'patch'.
'diff' and 'grep' would be a good idea, too, IMHO. And I might have
forgotten some things.

   Now follow the instructions in the FAQ you already posted. There's a
makefile/instruction file specifically for DJGPP in the MS-DOS system
directory, if I recall correctly.


> I believe the same executable it should work on both systems.

   Certainly, for text-mode. Again, I have no experience with tiles.
But yeah, once you get it compiled successfully, you can just stick it
on a floppy disk (memory stick, whatever) and carry it around. :)
Should work in any MS-DOS-or-later Microsoft OS.

